A mobile app is software with a specific purpose that you can install and run on mobile devices.

Mobile apps work on mobile devices, including smartphones, tablets, wearable devices, automobile infotainment devices, and eReaders like Kindle.

Apps provide different functionalities like help, notification, and inclusive user experience.

Apps may be designed to work on one or multiple device types.

A mobile app developer is a software developer with specialized skills, including knowledge of specific languages, frameworks, and tools used in mobile app development. 

App categories by the industry they service include utility apps for simple tasks, productivity apps for improving efficiency, connectivity apps to connect with other individuals or groups through text, voice, and video, social media and networking apps for networking, communication, and collaboration, health and fitness apps for tracking and monitoring physical and mental fitness, educational apps for helping users learn, shopping apps for viewing and purchasing items, news and entertainment apps for information across the world, business apps, for real-time business transactions 

Apps can be pre-installed, downloaded free of cost, or for a fee.

Apps can also be categorized based on platforms, business models, technology, or content.

The components of an app include front end, back end, database, and APIs.

Front end includes the user interface and the client-side logic for user interactions.

An app's back end manages the business logic, data processing, and server-side operations.

APIs enable communication between the front end and the back end.

The steps in processing a user request include user interaction with the app's UI on their mobile device, the front end sending a request to the backend server through APIs, the back end processing the request and preparing a response after interacting with the database as necessary, the back end sending the response back to the front end through APIs, and the front end receiving the response and updating the UI as required based on the response.

Developers can use cloud resources to create scalable, reliable, and secure mobile applications that meet user needs. 

Understanding how to host mobile services on the cloud effectively is crucial for the success of modern mobile apps. 

With cloud computing, the parts of a mobile app, including the front end, back end, APIs, and database, can work smoothly, providing a strong base for app functionality.

